{
  "schema": "mesence.cheat-intent-cases/1",
  "how_chosen": "Judged from CheatDb.Nes.json descriptions alone, with no play-testing. An entry is acceptable when its description, read literally, does what the intent asks. \"don't die\" accepts invincibility and infinite-health entries, but not infinite lives (with infinite lives you still die). \"infinite X\" accepts an entry that keeps X from running out, including a RAM write that pins X high, but not a \"... on pick-up\" entry. \"start on level/world N\" accepts only the entry for that N. NONE (accept: [\"NONE\"]) is the only correct answer when no description does what was asked - a level select in a game whose list has none, ammo in a game without ammo, or a request to invent a code. An entry and its \"(alt)\" twin are both acceptable, so both ids are listed where both exist. Independence: this set was authored without reading tests/fixtures/cheat-intent/intents.json, without reading scripts/cheat_intent_eval.py beyond its --help output, and without reading docs/validation/measurements/p11-cheat-intent-measurement-2026-10-02.md. The only input was UI/Dependencies/Internal/CheatDb.Nes.json. Intents are deliberately paraphrased, use synonym verbs and colloquial player phrasings, and are not near-literal restatements of any description; four intents are in pt-BR.",
